                        "form": "more snottery"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "ac31900c-61c1-4802-b946-aabacdfc61a4",
                        "entry_id": "fbe6aa47-4c0c-3933-b0f7-558ea326e8e3",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most snottery"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1d11add5-fd1e-3ddc-818e-7a5d7c01c409",
                        "entry_id": "fbe6aa47-4c0c-3933-b0f7-558ea326e8e3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Full of snot or phlegm; snotty."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d3ed487-a8b7-4a6d-a63a-2e827fdaf0fa",
                                "sense_id": "1d11add5-fd1e-3ddc-818e-7a5d7c01c409",
                                "text": "She didn't care about her snottery nose."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ba41fb6-5bc3-48b1-a8a6-28fb6e24cac5",
                                "sense_id": "1d11add5-fd1e-3ddc-818e-7a5d7c01c409",
                                "text": "\"We are about to enter a slavering, snottery, gnashing, bloody, excremental, universal madness, dear boy,\" he said gently."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f1b6a77-8880-4747-a011-59c7008697f8",
                                "sense_id": "1d11add5-fd1e-3ddc-818e-7a5d7c01c409",
                                "text": "It ate with a kind of baleful indifference, its wet, snottery trunk curling out mechanically to take the food through the bars."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d973bfb-2e47-41be-8f71-532bca85163d",
                                "sense_id": "1d11add5-fd1e-3ddc-818e-7a5d7c01c409",
                                "text": "She made a witty comment about tissues: at least it wasnt a snottery tissue like how some people leave their snottery tissues on the baize."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4acf1218-4e01-3619-8afd-669896128ba9",
                        "entry_id": "fbe6aa47-4c0c-3933-b0f7-558ea326e8e3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling or characteristic of snot."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f86b5fe8-5660-42ca-94aa-2a9812da874e",
                                "sense_id": "4acf1218-4e01-3619-8afd-669896128ba9",
                                "text": "A mistake in the kitchen one day, and while the rest of the household sup on the golden broth of a cockerel, out comes a bowl of thin, snottery gruel for Mhairi."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2465dd20-c70f-4595-bc93-62faecdb6208",
                                "sense_id": "4acf1218-4e01-3619-8afd-669896128ba9",
                                "text": "The old man sucked at his pipe, a great snottery, gurgling sound, and tamped down the black, oily tobacco with a horny forefinger, keeping up the suspense like the consummate showman that he was."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "22b648fe-ac70-4589-b366-f2a2a200b730",
                                "sense_id": "4acf1218-4e01-3619-8afd-669896128ba9",
                                "text": "I heard him laugh, a deep, snottery rumble, familiarly full of phlegm and juvenile amusement."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7b3065e3-fce5-32e8-8160-1c3e1f792b13",
                        "entry_id": "fbe6aa47-4c0c-3933-b0f7-558ea326e8e3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Presumptuous and demanding."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "86179906-b16c-4b86-a016-e4111bb60ba5",
                                "sense_id": "7b3065e3-fce5-32e8-8160-1c3e1f792b13",
                                "text": "\"You are in an unco' hurry,\" she replied, getting nettled, as she filled a glass. \"It doesna' do to be so snottery as a' that.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0439bfca-91c5-48a6-8a24-7998c644f7d5",
                                "sense_id": "7b3065e3-fce5-32e8-8160-1c3e1f792b13",
                                "text": "She still thought that, in a way, but she'd tell me in any case. I was, she explained, a snottery, two-faced wee shite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7cd0d71d-8127-4ece-be8c-41228322e328",
                                "sense_id": "7b3065e3-fce5-32e8-8160-1c3e1f792b13",
                                "text": "Una is turned into a right snottery wee brat, and she will need to mind her step."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "40177370-3b4d-34a1-b199-f4ae7e5c23da",
                "word": "snottery",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9df54cf3-a38a-4f5b-8947-039d5df19a5c",
                        "entry_id": "40177370-3b4d-34a1-b199-f4ae7e5c23da",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "snotteries"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "16b8b32c-58d4-3b6b-8bde-d63bdce55395",
                        "entry_id": "40177370-3b4d-34a1-b199-f4ae7e5c23da",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abomination; filth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "countable",
                            "rare",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "97dfc32a-339e-4b04-b484-f1b172052dba",
                                "sense_id": "16b8b32c-58d4-3b6b-8bde-d63bdce55395",
                                "text": "To purge the snottery of our slimy time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6f27cd0-5656-45c6-868d-93e6d60e4933",
                                "sense_id": "16b8b32c-58d4-3b6b-8bde-d63bdce55395",
                                "text": "She keeled the pot and swept away the dust. Changed the wet breechclouts, wiped the flowing snottery—And sometimes took a stroll as far as Shottery—"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "456dedc3-f12e-42c3-832c-d334e235b7d3",
                                "sense_id": "16b8b32c-58d4-3b6b-8bde-d63bdce55395",
                                "text": "For some reason (decades of responsibility to cleanliness and hygiene—what lady could blow her nose into a locust leaf?), the inability to place my hands on what would once have been a commonplace item unnerved me: were we to degenerate into filth and snottery?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "47c5ab8a-dadd-3885-94e2-c3912be64e46",
                        "entry_id": "40177370-3b4d-34a1-b199-f4ae7e5c23da",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Snobbishness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a78c6221-547a-446a-b62f-f676c709e577",
                                "sense_id": "47c5ab8a-dadd-3885-94e2-c3912be64e46",
                                "text": "[T]each thy Incubus to Poëtize, / And throvve abroad thy ſpurious Snotteries, / Vpon that puft-up Lumpe of Barmy froth, / […] / Or Clumſy Chil-blain'd Iudgement; that, vvith Oath, / Magnificates his Merit; and beſpaules / The conſcious Time, vvith humorous Fome; & bravvles, / As if his Organons of Senſe vvould crack / The ſinevves of my Patience."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d638d8b8-c1ff-4c55-954a-ce0dfa3b894c",
                                "sense_id": "47c5ab8a-dadd-3885-94e2-c3912be64e46",
                                "text": "In any case it would be nice to know if Neiman-Marcus, that famed emporium of chi-chi and snottery (see The New Yorker, its \"home away from home,\" any issue) and now Dallas's second most-celebrated landmark, purveys chamber-pots — \"His\" and \"Hers,\" let us say, cast in platinum or palladium (no gold, please, really, where have you been?), having diamond-studded handles (even Neiman-Marcus can't find anything more expensive than diamonds — no chips, of course) and emerald or sapphire eyes (with real lashes — gleaned from Elizabeth Taylor's coiffeur, naturally) encrusted in the bottoms."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b654465-3e04-415d-b834-8242d91e7757",
                                "sense_id": "47c5ab8a-dadd-3885-94e2-c3912be64e46",
                                "text": "Just you be careful, my girl, not to pick up a lotta snottery when you're over there among all them dudes. You got to keep your feet on the ground, and not get so's we can't understand a word you say."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ea804e9-1e4e-4591-94a5-5cd0342a01bc",
                                "sense_id": "47c5ab8a-dadd-3885-94e2-c3912be64e46",
                                "text": "He felt shock waves rumble through as he recognized his Sunday school snottery—how he thought he was better than other people, how he had a mighty swirly potty mouth, how at home he'd been on a six-month rampage about homework and chores, and how his sneaking out of the house had betrayed his parents."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
